A Style's font fields on android.

`fontSize` reached Compose's `TextStyle` and the other three did not.
`fontWeight` was compared against the string `"bold"`, which an enum member
never is, and `fontStyle` and `fontFamily` had no case at all -- so a heading
came out unemphasized on this target and a quotation upright, which is the
same defect fyne carried until this branch.

The three now go through the readers a run of rich text uses, a Style saying
them the same way a `markup.SpanStyle` does. `oblique` is italic, Compose
having upright and italic and no third face, and a family name that is not one
of the four generic ones falls back to the default: anything else is a font
resource an application registers, which SNGL has no way to name yet and which
would not compile if it were spelled as a lookup.

deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `style = TextStyle\(\)` -- a Style that sets nothing contributes no argument, rather than an empty one
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

window #home(title="fonts") {
    vbox {
        text(value="heavy", style={fontWeight=FontWeight.bold})
        text(value="light", style={fontWeight=FontWeight.lighter})
        text(value="slanted", style={fontStyle=FontStyle.italic})
        text(value="also slanted", style={fontStyle=FontStyle.oblique})
        text(value="code", style={fontFamily="monospace"})
        text(value="a face nobody registered", style={fontFamily="Comic Sans"})
        text(value="plain")
    }
}
-- out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt --
